From 1e1af07a8cd3d5ca9e7c7d59972cbcab3e96a0f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 08:43:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Second ratchet bounce: fixed number of ratchet notes and
 bounce without fade

Ratchet notes: Auto keeps the random 2/4/8 of 1.3, or always exactly 2 to 8 notes (at most 2 at 128th sync,
4 at 64th). Bounce fade: on keeps the v5 behaviour (later, shorter bounces softer), off keeps every note's
velocity. The defaults (Auto, fade on) behave exactly like v5. Evenly spaced ratchets now divide the step by
the number of notes, identical to before for 2, 4 and 8.
